{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvayRuC3orvLQZfkc4rq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Don't remove it yet. This data can't support that decision.**\n\n**Why the 4% is weak evidence**\n- **Missing data:** Five of 14 days (about 36%) of usage logging was broken. The 4% is probably an undercount, and by an unknown amount.\n- **No benchmark:** \"Low\" compared to what? Nobody seems to have set a target. A scheduling feature might reasonably start at 4%, or it might be a failure. Without a target, either reading is a guess.\n- **Weak metric:** \"Tried it\" measures curiosity and discoverability, not value. Repeat use, retention, and whether people keep the scheduled events matter more.\n- **Short window:** Two weeks at 10% exposure is early. Scheduling is an occasional task, so many users won't have needed it yet.\n\n**What I'd do**\n1. **Recover the data.** Look for sources that don't depend on the broken pipeline, such as server-side records of events created by auto-scheduling, raw logs, or database tables. Then recompute adoption.\n2. **Set the bar before looking.** Agree on the adoption, repeat-use, and retention thresholds that would justify keeping, iterating on, or removing the feature.\n3. **Look at depth, not just reach.** Among users who tried it, how many used it again, accepted the suggestions, or kept the events?\n4. **Check discoverability.** If the entry point is buried, low adoption says more about the UI than about the idea.\n5. **Get qualitative signal.** Support tickets, feedback, and a few user conversations are cheap and fast.\n6. **Pick a decision date.** Choose one or two more weeks of clean data, and keep the feature at 10% until then.\n\nKeeping it at 10% costs little and is easy to undo. Removing it is the costly, hard-to-reverse choice, so it needs better evidence than this."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3453,"cache_read_input_tokens":4979,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3453},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7e61b456-a894-4675-b0bd-599d077f8dc1","uuid":"5718893e-e709-4408-ae1d-2bea9b1cfb04","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:12:34.210Z","request_id":"req_011CfvayRfnfwSYJDoQSEfQT"}
